    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d570">

                <pb facs="1113" n="1101" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg1101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by General Chou En-lai to General
                        Marshall</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">MM 042</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-19">19 June 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear General Marshall</hi>: For your reference, on
                    June 9, two Nationalist regiments in North Liaoning laid terrible onslaught on
                    Faku (123°13′, 42°16′) and completely occupied that city in the afternoon of the
                    same date. Separate memo on this subject is being sent to General Hsu
                    Yung-chang, requesting that the Government military authority in Manchuria be
                    instructed to issue order for the evacuation of that city, so as to follow the
                    Lafa example, and to discharge the responsibility.<anchor n="25"
                        xml:id="d570-f1"/></p>
                <closer>[Signature in Chinese]<lb/>(<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chou
                            En-lai</hi></signed>)</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d570-f1" n="25" xml:id="d570-f1-content">
                <p>General Marshall reported this message in telegram No. 941, June 20, to Mr.
                    Robertson at Peiping and asked: “Have you a report of the alleged attack against
                    Faku? Do you think the proposed evacuation could be effected?</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
